#!/bin/sh
# Fake kubectl for tests: records the arguments and replies with the first rule
# (shell glob on the arguments) registered via `require("helpers").respond`.
printf '%s\n' "$*" >> "$KUBE_TEST_DIR/raw_calls"

# Record and match without --request-timeout, which nearly every call has
args=""
for arg in "$@"; do
  case "$arg" in
    --request-timeout=*) ;;
    *) args="${args:+$args }$arg" ;;
  esac
done
printf '%s\n' "$args" >> "$KUBE_TEST_DIR/calls"

if [ -f "$KUBE_TEST_DIR/rules" ]; then
  while IFS='	' read -r pattern script; do
    # shellcheck disable=SC2254
    case "$args" in
      $pattern) exec sh "$script" ;;
    esac
  done < "$KUBE_TEST_DIR/rules"
fi

echo "fake kubectl: no rule for: $args" >&2
exit 1
